    5. Ensure at least one frame has even interior area and one has odd. Interior area = (S-2)^2; even when S is even, odd when S is odd. If all same parity, swap one frame's S.
    6. Draw each frame as a 1-cell-thick blue border with black interior on a black grid.
    7. Output = input with each interior filled red (even area) or orange (odd area).
